WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.400 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
Harakiri is a self-hosted sandbox control plane for agent applications.

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:04.800 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
This is the real dashboard, at normal browser zoom. Follow a

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:07.200 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
release-check project from environment selection to verified cleanup.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:09.600 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
The example is deterministic: no model account or AI-generated output is

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:12.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
needed.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.500 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
Templates describe the environment your work runs in. Compare CPU,

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:21.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
memory, visibility and readiness before launching. This project uses

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:25.500 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
Node 20, with one CPU and 1 GiB of memory. Other agent-specific examples

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:30.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
live in the demo library; this tour focuses on the control plane itself.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.500 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
A workspace is persistent project storage, not another running sandbox.

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:39.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
Create release-checks once. Its files will be mounted at /workspace when

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:43.500 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
a sandbox attaches. This installation allocates 1 GiB; storage size and

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:48.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
availability depend on the operator configuration.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:53.500 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
Create a sandbox from the workspace. Choose Node 20, name the runtime

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:59.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
release-checks-01, and set a 30-minute lifetime for recording. Resources

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:04.500 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
come from the template. Internet access starts enabled. Provisioning may

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:10.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
take longer than shown: only waiting between chapters is removed.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:14.500 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
The sandbox detail view keeps status, lifetime, template and workspace

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:19.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
together. Terminal connects through Harakiri. Run pwd and node --version

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:23.500 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
to inspect the actual environment. Commands and outputs in this film are

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:28.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
executed, not reconstructed. There is no Kubernetes exec fallback.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:32.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
The example files were uploaded through the file API between chapters.

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:36.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
This minimal Node image needs curl and certificate roots for the

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:40.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
built-in access test. Run the included prepare-tools.sh through Commands

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:44.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
while Internet access is enabled. Package output is retained in

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:48.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
/tmp/tour-packages.log. A prepared team template can include these tools

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:52.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
already.

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:56.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
The four small example files are included with this tour. Filesystem

00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:00.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
shows the runtime directory listing, sizes and paths. Open /workspace to

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:04.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
inspect the project. This view is a browser, not an in-browser code

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:08.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
editor. The release check will create a report alongside these files.

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:13.600 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
Use Commands for tracked work. Set the working directory explicitly and

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:19.200 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
run node check.mjs. The script validates three release checks and writes

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:24.800 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
report.json. Output arrives while the command runs, and the exit code

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:30.400 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
makes completion explicit. This is a deterministic test fixture, not an

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:36.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
agent benchmark.

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:40.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
Move to Filesystem to see the new report, then return to Commands and

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:44.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
select the same run. Its output can be followed again without starting

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:48.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
duplicate work. Command history belongs to the runtime; it is not a

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:52.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
promise of permanent log retention after that runtime is deleted.

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:56.500 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
Start node server.mjs from Commands. It serves the report on port 3000

00:02:56.500 --> 00:03:01.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
and binds to all sandbox interfaces. The process continues when you move

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:05.500 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
to another tab. The UI gives tracked commands a five-minute command

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:10.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
timeout, so this preview is deliberately short-lived.

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:14.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
In Network, expose port 3000 as a Public route and open the resulting

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:18.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
URL. This example contains only synthetic release-check results. Public

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:22.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
means anyone with the URL can visit it; use Token access for a protected

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:26.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
service. The preview below is the actual running server, not a

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:30.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
screenshot mockup.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:35.600 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
Inbound previews and outbound policy solve different problems. Select

00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:41.200 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
the Node packages preset. The package registry is reachable; example.com

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:46.800 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
is not after the restriction. The capture verified that example.com was

00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:52.400 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
reachable before the change. Counters represent rules, not traffic

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:58.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
totals. These tests execute inside the sandbox.

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:01.600 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
Logs and Metrics keep runtime diagnostics near the work. Inspect

00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:05.200 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
lifecycle entries, then the current CPU and memory snapshot. These are

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:08.800 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
operational observations, not historical billing data or an

00:04:08.800 --> 00:04:12.400 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
agent-reasoning trace. Provider capabilities determine which additional

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:16.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
runtime measurements are available.

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:19.500 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
Kill terminates this sandbox and its preview route. It does not erase a

00:04:19.500 --> 00:04:23.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
persistent workspace. Wait for the workspace to finish releasing before

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:26.500 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
reusing it. The next chapter begins after that release has completed; no

00:04:26.500 --> 00:04:30.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
concurrent writer or instant handoff is implied.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:35.500 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
Return to Workspaces and create release-checks-02 from the same storage.

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:41.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
Choose Node 20 again. This is a new sandbox, not a resumed process or a

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:46.500 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
VM snapshot. The project files are retained; processes, open connections

00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:52.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
and command history are not carried over.

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:57.500 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
In the replacement sandbox, run the report verification command from

00:04:57.500 --> 00:05:03.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
/workspace. It reads the existing report.json and verifies that all

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:08.500 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
three checks passed. The capture also compares the report bytes across

00:05:08.500 --> 00:05:14.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
both runtimes. Nothing regenerates the report during this verification.

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:18.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
Terminate the replacement runtime and archive the workspace. The archive

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:22.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
dialog explicitly retains its files and storage allocation; physical

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:26.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
deletion is an operator action. Both runtimes and the preview are now

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:30.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
inactive. Continue with the CLI, SDK and OpenCode demos for real agent

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:34.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
workflows on the same control plane.
